WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.350
Do you know what’s going on in the earth
beneath your feet?

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.960
The world we know barely scratches the surface—and
far below, strange societies thrive in the

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.650
deepest and darkest of places.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:22.930
These are the tales of the modern-day societies
that live below the Earth’s surface.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:28.510
Buried under the streets of regal Paris lies
a most macabre underworld known as the Catacombs.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:33.950
This dusty ossuary holds the bones of over
six million people secure within the twisting

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.140
array of tunnels and caves.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.710
Its passages cover nearly three hundred and
twenty one kilometers of sprawling subterranean

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.190
real estate.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.920
One wrong turn, and you might find yourself
wandering among the dead for eternity.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.969
Originally, the Catacombs were a network of
tunnels dating back to the 13th century, the

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:58.250
remnants of the limestone mines, which caused
Paris to grow into the city we know today.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.140
By the 17th century, the burgeoning city had
filled all of its cemeteries to capacity,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.940
flooding the streets with the delightful aroma
of decaying flesh.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.020
Eau de corpse, anyone?

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.980
Towards the end of the 18th century, the situation
continued to deteriorate.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:19.520
King Louis the Fifteenth decided that enough
was enough—he decreed that no more burials

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:25.350
would be allowed within the city limits, though
due to resistance from the clergy the cemeteries

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.610
remained undisturbed.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:32.730
It wasn’t until the reign of Louis the Fifteenth’s
successor, Louis the Sixteenth, that the crusade

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.780
against the body odor made any progress.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.850
Louis the Sixteenth flexed his royal muscle
and declared that all cemeteries were to be

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:45.540
relocated outside of the city, but still the
clergy refused to budge.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:51.750
In 1780 torrential rains saturated the soil,
causing the bodies contained in one cemetery

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.160
to surface and spill onto the adjacent land.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:59.470
Thankfully, after this unfortunate event the
rest of the city agreed that something must

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.470
be done.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.020
It’s all fun and games until there’s a
body on your lawn.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.280
By 1798, the occupants of every cemetery in
the city had been moved by hand from their

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:15.720
former homes into their final resting places
within the catacombs—a job that certainly

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.580
no one would envy.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.450
The Catacombs saw use throughout the French
Revolution, and in 1860 the government finally

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.660
decided they had filled the tunnels sufficiently.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:30.280
Since then, the tunnels have been a haven
for urban explorers and others who wish to

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.390
haunt the gloom with the dead.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:37.530
Despite one of the entrances to the Catacombs
bearing a sign, which reads “Stop!

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.330
This is the empire of death!”

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.900
you can find many signs of life down there
today.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.920
In 2004, the Parisian Police stumbled upon
a bizarre complex within the Catacombs, complete

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:54.360
with electrical power, a cinema, a restaurant,
phone lines, and a closed circuit surveillance

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.360
system.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.560
If that isn’t the lair of a supervillain,
I don’t know what is.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.220
The place had seemingly been abandoned by
the time police discovered it, though there

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.940
were clear signs of recent occupation.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.220
When they returned three days later with city
infrastructure experts, they found that the

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:17.280
phone lines and power had been cut, and an
ominous note was left for them which read

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.090
“Do not try to find us”.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:26.060
Only a very small section of the catacombs
are open to the public, via guided tours only.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:31.680
The other mass expanse of sprawling tunnels
are strictly off limits, many explorers and

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.040
budding residents however use secret entrances
to access the Catacombs.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.720
Found in peculiar places such as in the basements
of bars and small gaps in the walls of the

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:47.590
metro tunnels, the locations of these secret
entrances are told to others only in strict

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:53.020
confidence to avoid the authorities finding
them and sealing them permanently.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:58.530
This secret network of illegal catacomb adventurers
are known as “Cataphiles”.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:03.970
They have to be secretive because accessing
the non-tourist area of the Catacombs is strictly

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.680
illegal and there’s a hefty fine if caught.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.800
If you do plan on plunging into the Catacombs
on an exploration of your own, be sure to

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.759
use the buddy system; this is one place you
do not want to get lost, because if you do

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:22.740
your chances of ever finding your way out
are virtually non-existent.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:28.090
Sequestered from the heat and sand of the
Mojave Desert, the Tunnel People of Las Vegas

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:31.780
carve out a living in the miles of flood tunnels
beneath the city.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:37.020
They live in a world of perpetual twilight,
eternally wary of the dangerous creatures

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:41.800
indigenous to the region, and the looming
threat of rain rushing in to wash away their

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.400
few possessions.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.460
The tunnels flood often and the Tunnel People
call the flood after a powerful rainstorm

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:55.000
“flushing the toilet”—they have to be
ever vigilant, ready to relocate at a moment’s

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.000
notice.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.940
Not exactly a sedentary lifestyle.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:03.780
Las Vegas has a reputation as the gleaming
gem of the desert—a beacon of civilization

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:09.160
and extravagance, where “what happens in
Vegas, stays in Vegas”.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.710
This also includes the people who pulled up
stakes and migrated their entire lives in

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:19.130
a moment to the asphalt oasis, only to discover
that making a living amongst the glittering

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:24.280
casinos and luxurious hotels wasn’t as easy
as they thought.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:29.570
Or perhaps a tragedy forced them out of a
secure lifestyle and on to the streets—either

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:34.860
way, these nomads usually find their way to
the flood tunnels to join the Tunnel People,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:40.210
making a living doing whatever odds and ends
they can in the bustling city above.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:44.919
Referred to as “normal people of all ages
who’ve lost their way”, their numbers

00:05:44.919 --> 00:05:50.930
include children, men and women struggling
with addiction, and even war veterans coping

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:53.520
with post-traumatic stress disorder.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:59.090
Despite their dire circumstances, the resilience
of the human spirit is evident in the culture

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:03.669
they’ve built for themselves, the tunnel
walls painted with elaborate graffiti art

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:07.990
and pieces of furniture designating rudimentary
“rooms” in the gloom.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:12.330
Though the Tunnel People live far beneath
the public eye and the glamour of the Vegas

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.550
Strip, they are not forgotten.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:19.050
The “Shine A Light” foundation, formed
by a journalist in partnership with the charity

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:23.940
HELP of Southern Nevada, brings necessities
like food and water to the tunnels, along

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.510
with blankets and other assistance.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:31.650
Bit by bit, the partnership works to improve
the lives of the impoverished Tunnel People—forming

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:35.720
a flickering light of hope in a very dark
place.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:41.710
Like the Tunnel People of Las Vegas, the inhabitants
of the Bucharest Sewers in Romania live in

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.510
a dimly lit underworld beneath the capital
city.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:50.479
They have access to a few more amenities than
their American counterparts, with electricity

00:06:50.479 --> 00:06:56.199
powering light bulbs, which dangle from the
ceiling in certain areas as well as other

00:06:56.199 --> 00:06:57.310
electronic luxuries.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.960
However, it’s not quite as cheery as it
might seem.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:05.150
Hidden away from the denizens of the capital
above ground, the people of the Bucharest

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.210
Sewers are true societal castaways.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:12.460
Though the citizens of Bucharest are aware
of the growing community beneath their feet,

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.330
few offer any kind of assistance.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:20.210
Nearly all of the members of the underworld
test HIV positive, with a large portion also

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.610
suffering from Tuberculosis.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:26.919
Despite the meager amount of light flooding
the hollows they call home, darkness lurks

00:07:26.919 --> 00:07:28.930
in every nook and cranny.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:33.800
The streets overhead can be a harsh place
to make a living—the sewers becoming somewhat

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.169
of a refuge, as they offer a modicum of safety
and warmth.

00:07:38.169 --> 00:07:42.460
And yet, the brutal reality of their life
continues to haunt the refugees within the

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:46.780
sheer concrete walls, many of them turning
to drugs as a means of escape.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:53.199
One man, who goes by the name “Bruce Lee”,
serves as the self-appointed vanguard of the

00:07:53.199 --> 00:07:54.199
sewers.

00:07:54.199 --> 00:07:58.009
He brings regular care packages of various
drugs and distributes them to all in need

00:07:58.009 --> 00:07:59.960
of a moment’s respite.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:04.139
Though it would be easy to consider him the
villain of this particular story, he has also

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:09.139
taken it upon himself to protect the children
down there from others who would bring them

00:08:09.139 --> 00:08:14.650
harm, as well as paying local city gangs to
stand sentry over the sewers and protect them

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.130
from antagonists.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:22.050
Sadly, life has become a game of “maintain
the status quo”, with little opportunity

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.600
for improvement.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:29.210
Aid organizations in Romania rely on funds
from overseas to continue their operations.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:34.479
Recently the monetary assistance has ceased
flowing into the country, rendering the relatively

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:37.729
small aid organizations impotent.

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:43.839
For the time being, life continues for Romania’s
Bucharest Sewer People as it has for years,

00:08:43.839 --> 00:08:48.379
fading into memory—with a steady stream
of drugs as a comping mechanism, and with

00:08:48.379 --> 00:08:50.779
only the barest of survival essentials.

00:08:50.779 --> 00:08:56.329
But as long as Bruce Lee rules over his simple
kingdom, perhaps they can take comfort in

00:08:56.329 --> 00:08:59.430
having some small measure of security.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:05.490
Rather than being driven underground by circumstances,
the farmers of the Loess Plateau in Yan’an,

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:11.350
China, choose to carve dwelling caves from
the earth out of convenience instead.

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:16.550
Evoking images of Luke Skywalker’s subterranean
home on Tatooine in the sci-fi spectacular

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:22.309
Star Wars, the farmers take advantage of the
plateau’s soft soil to dig traditional yaodong

00:09:22.309 --> 00:09:24.730
caves for themselves and their families.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:30.839
The yaodong are seen as important family heirlooms
to be passed from generation to generation.

00:09:30.839 --> 00:09:35.850
Many of them are now so old that the exact
number of generations who have occupied them

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:39.019
has been lost to the mists of time.

00:09:39.019 --> 00:09:43.309
Even if they can’t tell you who lived there
centuries ago, millions of people still call

00:09:43.309 --> 00:09:45.879
the caves homes to this day.

00:09:45.879 --> 00:09:50.670
Archeologists have determined that the people
of the Loess Plateau first began digging homes

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:57.259
during the Zhou Dynasty, between 1046 and
221 BC.

00:09:57.259 --> 00:10:02.680
Over the years, the cave dwellers came to
typify three varieties of yaodong: those dug

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:08.269
into cliffs, others set down into the soil,
and the last type being structures built partially

00:10:08.269 --> 00:10:11.230
into or against a mound of earth.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:15.749
Some of the cave dwellings came to incorporate
brick and stone into their design, and it’s

00:10:15.749 --> 00:10:20.269
these that proved to be the longest lasting,
some having been upgraded with modern amenities

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:21.269
and comforts.

00:10:21.269 --> 00:10:24.519
No word on whether they have fiber optic Internet
yet.

00:10:24.519 --> 00:10:30.389
Each family generally has between three and
five yaodong, with the one at the center serving

00:10:30.389 --> 00:10:33.569
as the main residence for the older members
of the family.

00:10:33.569 --> 00:10:38.059
Thanks to the insulative properties of the
earthen walls, the caves maintain a pleasant

00:10:38.059 --> 00:10:40.179
temperature all year round.

00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:46.149
No need for air conditioning or central heating—perhaps
the yaodong dwellers are on to something.

00:10:46.149 --> 00:10:51.399
The breathtaking yellow terrain of the Loess
Plateau and the many yaodong dotting the countryside

00:10:51.399 --> 00:10:55.000
have become a popular tourist attraction in
recent years.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.850
If you fancy a simple life of peace and plenty
whilst living in harmony with the earth, Yan’an

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:04.749
is one of the last places on earth where you
could carve your own life from the very ground

00:11:04.749 --> 00:11:06.950
beneath you with like-minded folks.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:11.899
Of course, you could try to dig a cave dwelling
elsewhere, but you might get some strange

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:12.899
looks.

00:11:12.899 --> 00:11:17.110
In 1969, the Chinese people were beginning
to feel the heat from the Cold War.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:22.819
Chairman Mao Zedong, sensing the growing potential
for overt hostility, decreed that tunnels

00:11:22.819 --> 00:11:27.779
and air-raid bunkers were to be built beneath
major cities—leading to the construction

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:32.459
of the areas now occupied by the “Rat Tribe”
of Beijing.

00:11:32.459 --> 00:11:36.369
Though the underground shelters were never
meant for prolonged occupation, they have

00:11:36.369 --> 00:11:42.019
become home to millions of citizens and migrant
workers who simply can’t afford to live

00:11:42.019 --> 00:11:43.689
in the city above.

00:11:43.689 --> 00:11:48.059
The “Rat Tribe” has since claimed many
of the city’s basements and other sublevels

00:11:48.059 --> 00:11:53.749
for rudimentary residences and hostels to
house the growing throng in need of cheap

00:11:53.749 --> 00:11:54.850
accommodation.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:58.449
Due to the cramped conditions, members of
the “Rat Tribe” often share bathrooms

00:11:58.449 --> 00:12:02.129
and kitchens, with thin walls separating them
from their neighbors.

00:12:02.129 --> 00:12:05.269
Not exactly the best place to practice your
karaoke I imagine.

00:12:05.269 --> 00:12:09.949
As a result of the construction projects and
infrastructure development brought about by

00:12:09.949 --> 00:12:16.809
the 2008 Beijing Olympics, thousands of migrants
were brought in to perform the manual labor.

00:12:16.809 --> 00:12:21.559
Left with no other options, many of them flocked
to the underground, where they were distinguished

00:12:21.559 --> 00:12:26.269
from the other inhabitants by the honorable
title of the “Ant Tribe” due to their

00:12:26.269 --> 00:12:30.299
industrious nature and the tiny spaces they
came to call home.

00:12:30.299 --> 00:12:35.490
In 2010, the government actually passed a
measure, which declared the underground community

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:40.380
illegal, which is just lovely, considering
government work, is why many of the migrants

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.459
are there in the first place.

00:12:42.459 --> 00:12:47.269
The government cited a desire to reclaim the
old air-raid shelters and refurbish them for

00:12:47.269 --> 00:12:48.860
public use.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:54.449
Over a hundred thousand people were evicted
from the underground in 2015, though previous

00:12:54.449 --> 00:12:58.869
efforts to close down the makeshift housing
and hostels of the “Rat Tribe” were met

00:12:58.869 --> 00:13:01.500
with unprecedented public protests.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:05.430
For now, the long-term prospects for the community
are in jeopardy.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.550
But as long as they aren’t forcibly removed
from the premises, the “Rat Tribe” will

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:14.499
continue to make the most of their simple,
yet cosy accommodations.

00:13:14.499 --> 00:13:19.209
Deep within the untamed outback of Australia
lies the town of Coober Pedy.

00:13:19.209 --> 00:13:24.980
After the 1915 discovery of opal gemstones
just waiting to be plucked from the arid soil,

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.350
the town sprang up almost overnight.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:33.069
The siren’s song of precious gems brought
people from all around the world to try their

00:13:33.069 --> 00:13:38.689
hand at mining—but they soon realised just
why the outback is so notorious.

00:13:38.689 --> 00:13:43.689
Sweltering temperatures assailed the fresh-faced
miners during the summer, while the winter

00:13:43.689 --> 00:13:48.629
saw temperatures plunge dramatically in mockery
of the former heat.

00:13:48.629 --> 00:13:52.850
Undaunted by the perilous environment, the
miners put their heads together to come up

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.359
with a solution.

00:13:54.359 --> 00:13:58.839
That solution, of course, was to move the
mining town underground.

00:13:58.839 --> 00:14:03.519
Though nobody cares to admit it, I suspect
some manner of venomous creature also had

00:14:03.519 --> 00:14:06.180
a hand in prompting relocation efforts.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.299
It is Australia, after all.

00:14:08.299 --> 00:14:13.049
Old mineshafts and new holes carved into the
sandstone became homes for the inhabitants

00:14:13.049 --> 00:14:14.519
of Coober Pedy.

00:14:14.519 --> 00:14:18.709
Especially in the early years most of the
digging was done by hand, though since then

00:14:18.709 --> 00:14:22.550
the task has been delegated to machinery better
suited for the work.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:28.629
As the 20th century rolled on the homes grew
more complex, some growing into hotels and

00:14:28.629 --> 00:14:33.790
inns to manage the tourists coming to bear
witness to the peculiar town.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:39.199
Modern Coober Pedy homes include all of the
expected amenities, like fully featured kitchens

00:14:39.199 --> 00:14:40.709
and walk-in closets.

00:14:40.709 --> 00:14:46.329
Besides housing, some dugouts became stores,
museums, and a church as well.

00:14:46.329 --> 00:14:51.009
Spending any amount of time in the unrelenting
heat of the Australian outback is bound to

00:14:51.009 --> 00:14:55.209
prompt prayers of a cool summer from even
the least religious person.

00:14:55.209 --> 00:15:01.709
Today, tourism rivals the opal as the foundation
upon which Coober Pedy’s economy lies.

00:15:01.709 --> 00:15:06.639
If you happen to find yourself in the area,
be sure to stop by the Underground Motel—a

00:15:06.639 --> 00:15:11.879
rare opportunity to experience the wonders
of living beneath the earth without committing

00:15:11.879 --> 00:15:14.269
wholeheartedly to the lifestyle.

00:15:14.269 --> 00:15:19.269
If you like it, who knows, maybe there’s
a dugout with your name on it.

